6847943	For the restoration of the verb &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;ari&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; &quot;it arrives&quot; with &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;annaš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; UD-&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;aš&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt; (&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;šiwaz&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;) as subject cf. the similar phrase in the treaty of Muwattalli II with Alakšandu of Wiluša CTH 76 KUB 21.1 i 64 &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;&lt;del_in/&gt;A-N&lt;del_fin/&gt;A&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;M&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;alakšandu&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;laes_in/&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;ŠA&lt;laes_fin/&gt;&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;AMA-&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;KA&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;UD&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;-az&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt;ari&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Hittite&gt; “&lt;del_in/&gt;But when&lt;del_fin/&gt; for (you), Alakšandu, the day of your mother arrives”. A remarkable feature is the left-dislocation of the ablative phrase &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt;IŠ-TU&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_AkkGRAM&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt;10&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;LÚ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;MEŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt;20&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Numeral&gt; &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;LÚ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_SumGRAM&gt;&lt;SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt;MEŠ&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_Determ&gt; and its resumption by the relative pronoun in the dat.-loc. pl. &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;kuedas&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_--italic&gt;. On the phenomenon of left-dislocation see &lt;SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;Hoffner H.A. − Melchert H.C. 2008a&lt;/SP_f_AO_3a_-LIT&gt;, 408f.
